 "_comment": "The tumbler allocator drift as the client's doctor row (nexus.health._check_next_seq_drift, over the live walk and the trash list) and the engine route GET /v1/catalog/owners/next_seq_drift (and the sweep POST /owners/sweep_next_seq_drift, which floors what this reports) both compute it; tests/catalog/test_next_seq_drift_cases.py runs this table through the client row and NextSeqDriftParityTest runs it through the route. An owner has drifted when its next_seq is STRICTLY below the highest numeric child sequence under its prefix, tombstoned children included; a child is '<prefix>.<digits>' (a deeper address and a non-digit tail are not children; a longer prefix is another owner); deactivated owners are examined. 'live' and 'tombstoned' name documents; expect.drifted lists the drifted owners in prefix order. WHAT IT DOES NOT PIN (Java tests only): the limit and capped flag, tenants, timeouts, and that the route writes nothing.",
